    <edge source="Regional CSCC" target="PET/CT">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">PET/CT scans are utilized in regional CSCC to evaluate whether the cancer has spread beyond regional lymph nodes.</data>
      <data key="d6">advanced imaging, metastasis detection</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regional CSCC" target="Head And Neck Tumors">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Head and neck tumors represent a critical manifestation of regional CSCC often requiring surgical removal of cervical lymph nodes.</data>
      <data key="d6">tumor localization, surgical oncology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regional CSCC" target="Surgery">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Surgery is considered the optimal primary treatment for regional CSCC to remove the primary tumor and involved lymph nodes.</data>
      <data key="d6">primary treatment, surgical intervention</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regional CSCC" target="Diagnostic Scans">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Diagnostic scans are employed to check whether regional CSCC has progressed into distant metastatic disease.</data>
      <data key="d6">staging, metastatic detection</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regional CSCC" target="NCCN">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">NCCN provides surveillance recommendations, including physical exams and imaging schedules, for regional CSCC patients.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical guidelines, cancer surveillance</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regional CSCC" target="Skin Exams">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Post-treatment surveillance for regional CSCC includes frequent skin examinations to check for cancer recurrence.</data>
      <data key="d6">surveillance protocol, physical examination</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb</data>
    </edge>
