    </edge>
    <edge source="Core Needle Biopsy" target="Biopsy">
      <data key="d4">53.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Core needle biopsy is a needle-based biopsy technique used to procure larger tissue specimens.&lt;SEP&gt;Core needle biopsy is a specialized needle technique used to extract tissue samples for biopsy.&lt;SEP&gt;Core needle biopsy is a specific method within the broader classification of biopsies.&lt;SEP&gt;Core needle biopsy is a specific sub-type of biopsy that uses a hollow needle to retrieve tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;Core needle biopsy is an established biopsy method used to remove tumor or lymph node samples for pathology.&lt;SEP&gt;Core needle biopsy is an established biopsy modality used to assess suspicious regional lymph nodes.</data>
      <data key="d6">biopsy method, tissue extraction&lt;SEP&gt;biopsy procedure, histological evaluation&lt;SEP&gt;classification, procedure variation&lt;SEP&gt;diagnostic classification, tissue sampling&lt;SEP&gt;procedural subtype, diagnostic sampling&lt;SEP&gt;sub-type, diagnostic procedure</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Core Needle Biopsy" target="Excisional Lymph Node Biopsy">
