    <edge source="Chronic Myeloid Leukemia" target="Philadelphia Chromosome">
      <data key="d4">30.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The Philadelphia chromosome is the cytogenetic cause of chronic myeloid leukemia; without it, CML is not diagnosed.&lt;SEP&gt;The Philadelphia chromosome is the diagnostic hallmark of CML and is present in individuals with this cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;The presence of the Philadelphia chromosome is required for a diagnosis of chronic myeloid leukemia.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic criterion, cytogenetic cause&lt;SEP&gt;diagnostic marker, causal factor&lt;SEP&gt;genetic hallmark, disease diagnostic</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chronic Myeloid Leukemia" target="BCR::ABL1">
      <data key="d4">30.0</data>
      <data key="d5">BCR::ABL1 produces an abnormal protein causing uncontrolled cell proliferation, making its inhibition the target of CML treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;The fused BCR::ABL1 gene is the specific genetic driver and causative mutation of chronic myeloid leukemia.&lt;SEP&gt;The presence of the BCR::ABL1 fusion gene is the defining diagnostic hallmark and molecular driver of chronic myeloid leukemia.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetic cause, oncogenesis&lt;SEP&gt;genetic driver, disease etiology&lt;SEP&gt;oncogenesis, targeted therapy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chronic Myeloid Leukemia" target="Myeloid Progenitor Cells">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Chronic myeloid leukemia arises from stem cells that generate an abnormal, increased quantity of myeloid progenitor cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease origin, cellular proliferation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chronic Myeloid Leukemia" target="Granulocytes">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Patients with chronic myeloid leukemia typically present with an overproduction of granulocytes.</data>
