    <edge source="Philadelphia Chromosome" target="BCR::ABL1">
      <data key="d4">30.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The Philadelphia chromosome and BCR::ABL1 fusion gene are both generated when pieces of chromosome 9 and 22 exchange positions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Philadelphia chromosome contains the fused BCR::ABL1 gene formed by the exchange between chromosomes 9 and 22.&lt;SEP&gt;Translocation between chromosomes 9 and 22 produces both the Philadelphia chromosome and the BCR::ABL1 fusion gene.</data>
      <data key="d6">chromosomal translocation, molecular genetics&lt;SEP&gt;genetic abnormality, chromosomal translocation&lt;SEP&gt;genetic fusion, chromosomal alteration</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Philadelphia Chromosome" target="BCR::ABL1 Gene">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The genetic translocation between chromosome 9 and chromosome 22 simultaneously forms the BCR::ABL1 fusion gene and the Philadelphia chromosome.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetic translocation, chromosomal alteration</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Philadelphia Chromosome" target="CML">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The Philadelphia chromosome is the hallmark chromosomal abnormality required for a definitive diagnosis of CML.</data>
      <data key="d6">biomarker, diagnostic hallmark</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Marrow" target="Blood Stem Cells">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
