    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Marrow" target="Hematopoietic Stem Cells">
      <data key="d4">36.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Bone marrow contains hematopoietic stem cells and serves as the primary organ site where blood cell formation takes place.&lt;SEP&gt;Bone marrow houses hematopoietic stem cells, which serve as the source of all blood cell development.&lt;SEP&gt;Hematopoietic stem cells reside in and are produced by the bone marrow to generate all bodily blood cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Hematopoietic stem cells reside within bone marrow tissue, where they originate and differentiate into blood lineages.</data>
      <data key="d6">cellular niche, hematopoiesis&lt;SEP&gt;cellular origin, biological synthesis&lt;SEP&gt;hematopoiesis, cellular origin&lt;SEP&gt;tissue habitat, hematopoiesis</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Marrow" target="Acute Myeloid Leukemia">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">AML arises within bone marrow across multiple bones, preventing the organ from producing healthy blood cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease origin, marrow pathology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Marrow" target="Lymphoblasts">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Bone marrow overproduces immature lymphoblasts during acute lymphoblastic leukemia, inhibiting healthy hematopoiesis.</data>
      <data key="d6">hematopoiesis, marrow crowding</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Marrow" target="Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Acute lymphoblastic leukemia affects bone marrow function by impairing the production of normal blood cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">bone marrow disease, leukemia manifestation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Marrow" target="High-Dose Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">High-dose chemotherapy wipes out both cancer cells and healthy stem cells within the bone marrow.</data>
      <data key="d6">myeloablation, marrow destruction</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Marrow" target="Stem Cell Replacement">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Transfused stem cells migrate to the bone marrow where they engraft and regenerate healthy blood cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">marrow engraftment, tissue regeneration</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Marrow" target="B Cells">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">B cells originate and mature within the bone marrow before entering the bloodstream and lymphatic network.</data>
      <data key="d6">hematopoiesis, cellular origin</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Blood Stem Cells" target="Progenitor Cells">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Blood stem cells produce progenitor cells as intermediaries in the process of cell differentiation.</data>
      <data key="d6">cellular differentiation, hematopoiesis</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Blood Stem Cells" target="Lymphoid Progenitor Cells">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Blood stem cells differentiate into lymphoid progenitor cells during hematopoiesis.</data>
      <data key="d6">cellular differentiation, hematopoiesis&lt;SEP&gt;hematopoiesis, cell differentiation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Blood Stem Cells" target="Myeloid Progenitor Cells">
      <data key="d4">26.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Blood stem cells give rise to myeloid progenitor cells during hematopoiesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood stem cells give rise to myeloid progenitor cells during the process of blood formation.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood stem cells produce an increased amount of myeloid progenitor cells during the pathogenesis of CML.</data>
      <data key="d6">cellular differentiation, hematopoiesis&lt;SEP&gt;differentiation, hematopoiesis&lt;SEP&gt;hematopoiesis, cell proliferation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Blood Stem Cells" target="Red Blood Cells">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Blood stem cells mature and differentiate into red blood cells in the bone marrow.</data>
      <data key="d6">hematopoiesis, cell lineage</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Blood Stem Cells" target="Platelets">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Blood stem cells develop through precursor stages to produce functional platelets.</data>
      <data key="d6">hematopoiesis, cell lineage</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Blood Stem Cells" target="White Blood Cells">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Blood stem cells serve as the common origin for all classes of white blood cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">hematopoiesis, cell lineage</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Blood Stem Cells" target="CML">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">CML is thought to arise from blood stem cells that generate excessive myeloid progenitor cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease origin, oncogenesis</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Progenitor Cells" target="Myeloid Progenitor Cells">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Myeloid progenitor cells are a specific class of progenitor cells that mature into myeloid lineages.&lt;SEP&gt;Myeloid progenitor cells represent a primary lineage branch of intermediary precursor cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">cell classification, lineage commitment&lt;SEP&gt;lineage branch, precursor subtype</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Progenitor Cells" target="Lymphoid Progenitor Cells">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Lymphoid progenitor cells are a subtype of progenitor cells that develop into lymphoid lineages.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphoid progenitor cells represent one of the major lineages of hematopoietic progenitor cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">cell classification, lineage commitment&lt;SEP&gt;lineage branch, precursor subtype</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Progenitor Cells" target="Blood Cells">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Hematopoietic progenitor cells undergo differentiation to produce mature red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets.</data>
      <data key="d6">hematopoiesis, cell differentiation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Progenitor Cells" target="Hematopoietic Stem Cells">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Hematopoietic stem cells produce intermediary precursor cells known as progenitor cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">lineage development, stem cell differentiation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Myeloid Progenitor Cells" target="Hematopoietic Stem Cells">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Hematopoietic stem cells differentiate into myeloid progenitor cells during hematopoiesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Hematopoietic stem cells differentiate into myeloid progenitor cells to generate non-lymphoid blood lineages.</data>
      <data key="d6">cell differentiation, hematopoiesis&lt;SEP&gt;differentiation, cellular lineage</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Myeloid Progenitor Cells" target="Acute Myeloid Leukemia">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">AML disrupts the maturation process of myeloid progenitor cells, leading to abnormal blast formation.&lt;SEP&gt;Acute Myeloid Leukemia targets and disrupts the myeloid progenitor cell lineage, generating abnormal myeloblasts.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease origin, oncogenesis&lt;SEP&gt;pathophysiology, cell differentiation</data>
