      <data key="d5">Myeloid progenitor cells differentiate into myeloblasts which mature into granulocytes.</data>
      <data key="d6">cell maturation, lineage progression</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lymphoid Progenitor Cells" target="Hematopoietic Stem Cells">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Hematopoietic stem cells differentiate into lymphoid progenitor cells during hematopoiesis.</data>
      <data key="d6">cell differentiation, hematopoiesis</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lymphoid Progenitor Cells" target="Lymphoblasts">
      <data key="d4">27.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Lymphoid progenitor cells develop into lymphoblasts as part of blood cell maturation.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphoid progenitor cells directly develop into lymphoblasts during lymphocyte maturation.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphoid progenitor cells form lymphoblasts, which ordinarily mature into lymphocytes.</data>
      <data key="d6">cell development, lineage&lt;SEP&gt;cell lineage, hematopoiesis&lt;SEP&gt;cellular progression, maturation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lymphoid Progenitor Cells" target="Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Acute lymphoblastic leukemia is believed to originate from abnormal proliferation of lymphoid progenitor cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Acute lymphoblastic leukemia is thought to arise from abnormalities in lymphoid progenitor cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease origin, oncogenesis&lt;SEP&gt;oncogenesis, disease origin</data>
