    </edge>
    <edge source="White Blood Cells" target="Granulocytes">
      <data key="d4">35.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Granulocytes are a major category of white blood cells that protect the body against infection.&lt;SEP&gt;Granulocytes are a primary subtype of white blood cells involved in immune defense.&lt;SEP&gt;Granulocytes represent one of the main subtypes of white blood cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Granulocytes, consisting of neutrophils, eosinophils, and basophils, are a primary subtype of white blood cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">biological classification, immune system&lt;SEP&gt;cell classification, immune system&lt;SEP&gt;cellular classification, leukocyte composition&lt;SEP&gt;subtyping, cellular classification</data>
