    <edge source="Platelets" target="Hematopoietic Stem Cells">
      <data key="d4">24.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Hematopoietic stem cells develop and mature into blood platelets to prevent bleeding.&lt;SEP&gt;Hematopoietic stem cells in the bone marrow differentiate to form functional platelets that assist with blood clotting.&lt;SEP&gt;Hematopoietic stem cells produce platelets essential for hemostasis.</data>
      <data key="d6">hematopoiesis, cell development&lt;SEP&gt;hematopoiesis, cell maturation&lt;SEP&gt;lineage development, hematopoiesis</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Platelets" target="Lymphoblasts">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Excessive numbers of lymphoblasts crowd out platelets in bone marrow, hindering bleeding control.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease impact, cellular crowding</data>
