      <data key="d6">medical practice, treatment prescription</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chemoradiation" target="Watch And Wait">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The watch and wait strategy is considered if chemoradiation effectively eradicates cancer signs.</data>
      <data key="d6">monitoring strategy, response assessment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chemoradiation" target="Locally Advanced Cancer">
      <data key="d4">27.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Chemoradiation is the standard therapy recommended for locally advanced cervical cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Locally advanced cervical cancer is primarily managed with chemoradiation therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Locally advanced rectal cancers are typically treated using chemoradiation.</data>
      <data key="d6">stage-specific therapy, concurrent treatment&lt;SEP&gt;standard care, oncologic therapy&lt;SEP&gt;standard treatment, oncological management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chemoradiation" target="Cervical Cancer">
      <data key="d4">26.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Chemoradiation is designated as one of the principal treatment modalities for cervical cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemoradiation is the standard recommended treatment modality for locally advanced cervical cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemoradiation is the standard treatment strategy recommended for most locally advanced cervical cancers.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer therapy, treatment recommendation&lt;SEP&gt;cancer treatment, multimodality therapy&lt;SEP&gt;cancer treatment, therapeutic protocol</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chemoradiation" target="Locally Advanced Cervical Cancer">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Chemoradiation is specifically recommended as the standard treatment for locally advanced cervical cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemoradiation is the standard recommended treatment protocol for patients with locally advanced cervical cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical standard, disease management&lt;SEP&gt;standard care, clinical recommendation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chemoradiation" target="Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d4">45.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Chemoradiation incorporates chemotherapy as a concurrent treatment element alongside radiation.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy constitutes the medicinal component within a multimodal chemoradiation protocol.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy is administered concurrently alongside radiation therapy as part of chemoradiation.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy is administered concurrently once weekly alongside radiation in chemoradiation protocols.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy is an essential concurrent component administered alongside radiation therapy in chemoradiation regimens.</data>
      <data key="d6">combined modality, therapeutic synergy&lt;SEP&gt;concurrent therapy, treatment combination&lt;SEP&gt;treatment combination, oncology&lt;SEP&gt;treatment component, combination therapy&lt;SEP&gt;treatment component, systemic therapy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chemoradiation" target="Radiation Therapy">
      <data key="d4">53.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Chemoradiation combines radiation therapy with chemotherapy to treat anal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemoradiation combines radiation therapy with chemotherapy to treat bladder cancer more effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemoradiation couples radiation therapy with chemotherapy to enhance tumor response.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemoradiation incorporates external beam radiation therapy given concurrently with chemotherapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Radiation therapy forms the targeted radiotherapeutic component of chemoradiation.&lt;SEP&gt;Radiation therapy is one of the two core simultaneous modalities comprising chemoradiation.</data>
      <data key="d6">combination therapy, treatment protocol&lt;SEP&gt;combined therapy, synergistic treatment&lt;SEP&gt;combined treatment, therapeutic synergy&lt;SEP&gt;treatment combination, radiation oncology&lt;SEP&gt;treatment component, combination therapy&lt;SEP&gt;treatment component, combined modality</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chemoradiation" target="Systemic Therapy">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Chemoradiation utilizes systemic platinum-based chemotherapy administered alongside radiation.</data>
      <data key="d6">combination therapy, systemic treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chemoradiation" target="Stage 1B3">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Chemoradiation is the preferred frontline treatment option for stage 1B3 cervical cancers.</data>
      <data key="d6">definitive treatment, preferred therapy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chemoradiation" target="Stage 2A2">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Stage 2A2 tumors larger than 4 cm are primarily managed with chemoradiation and brachytherapy.</data>
      <data key="d6">preferred therapy, standard of care</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chemoradiation" target="Systemic Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Chemoradiation incorporates chemotherapy along with radiation therapy to produce better treatment outcomes than chemotherapy alone.</data>
      <data key="d6">combined therapy, multimodal treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chemoradiation" target="Trimodal Therapy">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
