      <data key="d7">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Breast Cancer" target="Genetic Risk Testing">
      <data key="d4">15.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Genetic risk testing identifies inherited mutations that account for approximately 1 out of 10 breast cancers.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic risk testing identifies inherited predispositions and risk factors for hereditary breast cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetics, risk assessment&lt;SEP&gt;hereditary cancer, genetic susceptibility</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Breast Cancer" target="Breast Exam">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Physical palpation of the breast and armpit during an exam helps detect abnormalities indicative of breast cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical screening, symptom detection</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Breast Cancer" target="Contraception">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Non-hormonal contraception methods like barrier devices and IUDs are preferred for patients with breast cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">contraindication management, reproductive health</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Breast Cancer" target="Diagnostic Mammogram">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Diagnostic mammograms are used to detect tumors, determine tumor size, and plan treatment for breast cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">pathology detection, diagnostic utility</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Breast Cancer" target="Spine And Brain MRI">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Spine and brain MRIs are conducted to evaluate whether breast cancer has metastasized to the central nervous system.</data>
      <data key="d6">metastasis detection, staging</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Breast Cancer" target="Biomarker Testing">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Biomarker testing is utilized in breast cancer management to evaluate tumor characteristics and determine tailored treatment options.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic application, cancer care</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Breast Cancer" target="BRCA Tests">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Mutations identified through BRCA tests significantly increase the risk of developing breast cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer risk, hereditary factors</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Breast Cancer" target="Endocrine Therapy">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Endocrine therapy is utilized to treat hormone receptor-positive breast cancer by blocking hormones that stimulate tumor growth.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease treatment, oncology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Breast Cancer" target="PARP Inhibitors">
