    </edge>
    <edge source="Smoking" target="Bladder Cancer">
      <data key="d4">27.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Smoking is considered the primary risk factor for bladder cancer, accounting for roughly 50% of cases.&lt;SEP&gt;Smoking represents the single greatest risk factor associated with developing bladder cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Smoking significantly elevates the risk of developing bladder cancer and triples the risk of dying from it.</data>
