    </edge>
    <edge source="Lymphocytes" target="Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia">
      <data key="d4">45.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Acute lymphoblastic leukemia arises from lymphoid progenitor cells that normally differentiate into lymphocytes.&lt;SEP&gt;Acute lymphoblastic leukemia arises within immune system white blood cells known as lymphocytes.&lt;SEP&gt;Acute lymphoblastic leukemia develops when bone marrow produces an excessive number of immature lymphocytes called lymphoblasts.&lt;SEP&gt;Acute lymphoblastic leukemia directly impacts lymphocytes through the proliferation of immature lymphoblasts.&lt;SEP&gt;Acute lymphoblastic leukemia is a fast-growing cancer that originates within immune system lymphocytes.</data>
      <data key="d6">cellular origin, hematologic malignancy&lt;SEP&gt;cellular origin, hematopoiesis&lt;SEP&gt;cellular origin, leukemia pathology&lt;SEP&gt;cellular origin, pathology&lt;SEP&gt;disease manifestation, cellular pathology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lymphocytes" target="Lymphoblasts">
      <data key="d4">25.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Lymphoblasts are immature precursor cells that differentiate into mature lymphocytes.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphoblasts are immature precursor cells that normally mature into functional lymphocytes.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphoblasts mature into functional lymphocytes in normal hematopoiesis.</data>
      <data key="d6">cell maturation, immune development&lt;SEP&gt;cellular development, maturation&lt;SEP&gt;cellular maturation, immunology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lymphocytes" target="B Cells">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">B cells are one of the primary types of lymphocytes in the immune system.&lt;SEP&gt;B cells are one of the three primary functional types of lymphocytes.</data>
      <data key="d6">cell classification, immune taxonomy&lt;SEP&gt;cellular classification, lymphocyte subtype</data>
