      <data key="d6">viral etiology, oncogenesis</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nasopharyngeal Cancer" target="NCCN">
      <data key="d4">15.0</data>
      <data key="d5">NCCN offers patient guidelines and educational resources regarding nasopharyngeal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;NCCN provides staging guides, TNM scores, and educational resources regarding nasopharyngeal cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical guidelines, cancer staging&lt;SEP&gt;patient resources, disease guidance</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nasopharyngeal Cancer" target="Head and Neck Cancers">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Nasopharyngeal cancer is an anatomical subtype of head and neck cancer originating in the nasopharynx.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease subtype, anatomy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nasopharyngeal Cancer" target="Eye Exam">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Nasopharyngeal cancer can affect the eyes, prompting the recommendation for an eye exam prior to therapy.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease manifestation, diagnostic screening</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nasopharyngeal Cancer" target="EBV-Related Cancer">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The vast majority of nasopharyngeal cancers are categorized as EBV-related cancers caused by Epstein-Barr virus.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease classification, viral etiology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nasopharyngeal Cancer" target="Biomarker Testing">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Biomarker testing on tumor and blood samples is performed to determine treatments and detect EBV DNA in nasopharyngeal cancer patients.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic testing, treatment planning</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nasopharyngeal Cancer" target="Tumor HPV Testing">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">HPV testing may be conducted in select cases of nasopharyngeal cancer to determine viral etiology.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic testing, tumor evaluation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nasopharyngeal Cancer" target="Cancer Staging">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Nasopharyngeal cancer staging determines the severity of NPC, defines prognosis, and guides therapy selection.</data>
      <data key="d6">prognosis, treatment planning</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Volume Center" target="Pancreatic Cancer">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
