    </edge>
    <edge source="Family History" target="Care Team">
      <data key="d4">23.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The care team asks questions regarding family health history to identify potential hereditary diseases and cancer risks.&lt;SEP&gt;The care team gathers and reviews family history to assess hereditary cancer risks and related conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;The care team gathers family health history to check for familial disease patterns and genetic considerations.</data>
      <data key="d6">health history, genetic risk&lt;SEP&gt;risk assessment, clinical inquiry&lt;SEP&gt;risk assessment, patient history</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Family History" target="Genetic Testing">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Family history assessments inquire whether blood relatives have previously undergone genetic testing.</data>
      <data key="d6">hereditary assessment, genetic history</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Family History" target="AML">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Family history assesses familial cancer occurrences to provide context for genetic testing and risk factors associated with AML.</data>
      <data key="d6">hereditary risk, genetic testing</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Family History" target="Ovarian Cancer">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A family history of ovarian cancer contributes to an increased risk profile for prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">hereditary risk, cancer genetics</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Family History" target="Colon Cancer">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Family patterns of colon cancer are identified as relevant family history factors linked to cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d6">familial risk, shared risk factors</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Family History" target="Genetic Cancer Risk Testing">
      <data key="d4">25.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A family history of cancer and other hereditary diseases directly informs the need for genetic cancer risk testing.&lt;SEP&gt;A family history of cancer informs the need for and evaluation of genetic cancer risk testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Family health history guides decisions on whether genetic cancer risk testing is warranted.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetic risk, inherited traits, diagnostic assessment&lt;SEP&gt;hereditary risk, clinical assessment&lt;SEP&gt;hereditary risk, genetic assessment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Family History" target="Bone Cancer">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Family history assessment aids in identifying genetic cancer risk and context during bone cancer diagnosis and care planning.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetic risk, clinical assessment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Family History" target="Doctor">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The doctor asks patients about the medical history of blood relatives to evaluate hereditary disease risk.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical assessment, family screening</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Family History" target="Bladder Cancer">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Having a family history of bladder cancer elevates an individual's personal risk of developing the disease.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetic risk factor, heredity</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Tobacco And Alcohol Use" target="Care Team">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The care team assesses tobacco and alcohol history and provides resources to quit smoking and limit alcohol.</data>
      <data key="d6">patient assessment, lifestyle intervention</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Tobacco And Alcohol Use" target="Head And Neck Cancers">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Tobacco and alcohol use are major risk factors that drive the development of head and neck cancers and worsen treatment outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d6">etiology, cancer risk factors</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
