    <edge source="Dental Exam" target="Dentist">
      <data key="d4">26.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A dentist performs dental exams and necessary dental work before certain cancer therapies commence.&lt;SEP&gt;Dentists conduct dental exams and cleanings to evaluate oral health and prevent complications related to head and neck cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;The dentist performs the dental exams, cleanings, and procedures needed prior to initiating head and neck cancer therapies.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical evaluation, preventive dentistry&lt;SEP&gt;dental evaluation, medical care&lt;SEP&gt;oral healthcare, provider responsibility</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Dental Exam" target="Head And Neck Cancers">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Dental exams are critical prior to and during head and neck cancer treatment to preserve oral cavity and jaw health.</data>
      <data key="d6">supportive care, clinical evaluation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Endoscopy With Examination Under Anesthesia" target="Pre-Anesthesia Exam">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A pre-anesthesia exam is conducted prior to procedures requiring anesthesia, such as endoscopy with EUA.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical prerequisite, surgical safety</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FDG-PET/CT" target="CT Scan">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">FDG-PET/CT combines PET scanning with CT imaging into a single diagnostic procedure.&lt;SEP&gt;FDG-PET/CT incorporates CT technology and can be executed simultaneously with diagnostic CT imaging.</data>
      <data key="d6">combined modality, imaging procedure&lt;SEP&gt;multimodal imaging, cancer evaluation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FDG-PET/CT" target="Bone Scan">
      <data key="d4">23.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A clear FDG-PET/CT result confirming bone cancer can eliminate the need for a separate bone scan.&lt;SEP&gt;A conclusive FDG-PET/CT scan showing bone involvement may eliminate the need for a separate bone scan.&lt;SEP&gt;Clear evidence of bone metastasis on FDG-PET/CT can render a conventional bone scan unnecessary.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic alternative, clinical decision-making&lt;SEP&gt;diagnostic substitution, clinical evaluation&lt;SEP&gt;diagnostic substitution, staging efficiency</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FDG-PET/CT" target="Sodium Fluoride PET/CT">
      <data key="d4">23.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A decisive FDG-PET/CT showing bone metastasis can eliminate the need for a supplementary sodium fluoride PET/CT.&lt;SEP&gt;An FDG-PET/CT scan can replace the need for sodium fluoride PET/CT when bone metastasis is definitively shown.&lt;SEP&gt;Clear findings on an FDG-PET/CT scan can replace the need for sodium fluoride PET/CT scans.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic alternative, clinical decision-making&lt;SEP&gt;diagnostic substitution, imaging protocol&lt;SEP&gt;diagnostic substitution, nuclear imaging</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FDG-PET/CT" target="Extramedullary Leukemia">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">FDG-PET/CT imaging is utilized to identify leukemia located outside the bone marrow and blood.&lt;SEP&gt;FDG-PET/CT is used to visualize extramedullary leukemia when cancer cells spread outside the blood and marrow.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease localization, diagnostic imaging&lt;SEP&gt;imaging, cancer staging</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FDG-PET/CT" target="AML">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">FDG-PET/CT is recommended in AML to detect extramedullary disease.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer detection, staging</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FDG-PET/CT" target="Fluorodeoxyglucose">
      <data key="d4">28.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Fluorodeoxyglucose is the radiotracer injected into a vein to perform an FDG-PET/CT scan.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluorodeoxyglucose is the specific radiotracer agent employed during FDG-PET/CT scans to highlight cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluorodeoxyglucose serves as the primary radioactive drug utilized in FDG-PET/CT scans to detect active cancer cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">radiopharmaceutical agent, diagnostic imaging&lt;SEP&gt;radiotracer agent, imaging diagnostic&lt;SEP&gt;tracer component, metabolic imaging</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FDG-PET/CT" target="Distant Metastases">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">FDG-PET/CT scans are utilized to detect whether nasopharyngeal carcinoma has spread to form distant metastases.</data>
      <data key="d6">metastasis detection, oncology imaging</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FDG-PET/CT" target="Nasopharyngeal Carcinoma">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">FDG-PET/CT is performed during treatment planning for nasopharyngeal carcinoma to identify metastatic disease.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer staging, diagnostic imaging</data>
