    <edge source="Fertility Preservation" target="Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d4">43.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Because chemotherapy can permanently impair reproductive ability, fertility preservation must be discussed prior to treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy can impair fertility, making proactive consultation about fertility preservation necessary before starting treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy can impair fertility, prompting the need for proactive discussions about fertility preservation.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy can impair fertility, prompting the need for proactive fertility preservation consultations.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy treatments carry risks of long-term infertility, necessitating fertility preservation discussions before therapy.</data>
      <data key="d6">adverse effects, reproductive health&lt;SEP&gt;gonadotoxicity, reproductive preservation&lt;SEP&gt;reproductive risk, preventive intervention&lt;SEP&gt;treatment side effects, fertility risk&lt;SEP&gt;treatment toxicity, reproductive risk</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Fertility Preservation" target="Targeted Therapy">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Fertility preservation is evaluated prior to starting targeted therapy due to potential impacts on reproductive ability.&lt;SEP&gt;Targeted therapies may negatively impact patient fertility, requiring discussions about fertility preservation.</data>
