    </edge>
    <edge source="Fertility Preservation" target="Contraception">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Contraception is essential alongside fertility management to prevent fetal harm caused by cancer therapies.&lt;SEP&gt;Contraceptive options are coordinated during cancer therapy to prevent pregnancy while preserving long-term reproductive safety.</data>
      <data key="d6">pregnancy prevention, reproductive safety&lt;SEP&gt;reproductive health, treatment safety</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Fertility Preservation" target="Radiation Therapy">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Radiation therapy damages ovarian and testicular function, prompting the need for counseling and fertility preservation procedures.</data>
