      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Acute myeloid leukemia is identified as a rare, severe side effect of maintenance therapy using PARP inhibitors.</data>
      <data key="d6">adverse effect, hematologic complication</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Acute Myeloid Leukemia" target="Myelodysplastic Syndrome">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Myelodysplastic syndrome can progress into acute myeloid leukemia in certain clinical cases.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease progression, malignancy evolution</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Acute Myeloid Leukemia" target="Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Both AML and ALL are acute forms of blood and bone marrow cancers addressed in oncology care guides.</data>
      <data key="d6">hematologic malignancies, blood cancer</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Acute Myeloid Leukemia" target="Stem Cells">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Acute myeloid leukemia originates within the stem cells of the bone marrow.</data>
      <data key="d6">cellular origin, hematologic malignancy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Acute Myeloid Leukemia" target="Blood Cancer">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Acute myeloid leukemia is classified as a specific type of blood cancer arising from bone marrow stem cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease classification, oncology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Acute Myeloid Leukemia" target="Hematopoietic Stem Cells">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Acute myeloid leukemia originates in the blood-forming stem cells of the bone marrow.</data>
      <data key="d6">oncogenesis, disease origin</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Acute Myeloid Leukemia" target="Bone Marrow Test">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A bone marrow test is required to definitively diagnose acute myeloid leukemia before initiating treatment.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic procedure, disease diagnosis</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Acute Myeloid Leukemia" target="Coagulation Panel">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Coagulation panels screen for clotting abnormalities and coagulopathy, which are common complications in leukemia.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical monitoring, complications</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Acute Myeloid Leukemia" target="White Blood Cell Differential">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A differential test evaluates white blood cell proportions and can identify circulating leukemia blasts.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic testing, leukemia detection</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Acute Myeloid Leukemia" target="Performance Status Scales">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Performance status scales are evaluated to understand the patient's general health when selecting an AML treatment regimen.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment planning, patient evaluation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Acute Myeloid Leukemia" target="AML Genetic Changes">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Specific acquired genetic alterations in leukemic cells define AML subtypes, assist in determining prognosis, and direct targeted therapy.</data>
      <data key="d6">genomic profiling, targeted treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Acute Myeloid Leukemia" target="Karnofsky Performance Status">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The Karnofsky Performance Status is evaluated to determine a patient's fitness for AML treatment regimens.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical evaluation, treatment selection</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Acute Myeloid Leukemia" target="Hematopathology Review">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Hematopathology review of bone marrow cells provides definitive cellular diagnosis and classification of AML.</data>
      <data key="d6">pathological evaluation, cancer confirmation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Acute Myeloid Leukemia" target="Molecular Testing">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Molecular testing helps determine AML prognosis, disease subtype, and targets for treatment.</data>
      <data key="d6">prognostic assessment, targeted therapy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Acute Myeloid Leukemia" target="Imaging Tests">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Imaging tests identify whether leukemia has spread to extra-medullary sites such as the liver, spleen, lymph nodes, or central nervous system.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease staging, cancer surveillance</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Acute Myeloid Leukemia" target="RUNX1::RUNX1T">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">RUNX1::RUNX1T is a genetic abnormality and predisposition marker evaluated in acute myeloid leukemia.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetic alteration, leukemia pathology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Acute Myeloid Leukemia" target="Care Team">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The multidisciplinary care team collaborates with the patient to manage diagnosis and treatment plans for acute myeloid leukemia.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease management, clinical oversight</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Acute Myeloid Leukemia" target="Targeted Therapy">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Targeted therapies are selected based on genetic and biomarker testing of acute myeloid leukemia subtypes.&lt;SEP&gt;Targeted therapies such as gemtuzumab ozogamicin, gilteritinib, and quizartinib are utilized to treat acute myeloid leukemia with specific mutations.</data>
      <data key="d6">oncological treatment, precision medicine&lt;SEP&gt;precision medicine, targeted oncology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Acute Myeloid Leukemia" target="Hematopoietic Cell Transplant">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
