      <data key="d7">chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AML" target="Hypomethylating Agents">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Hypomethylating agents are used to treat AML by blocking excessive methyl groups on DNA to allow leukemic cells to mature.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease management, targeted mechanism</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AML" target="Targeted Therapy">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Targeted therapies are tailored to specific molecular characteristics or mutations present in AML, such as FLT3 mutations or CD33 markers.</data>
      <data key="d6">precision medicine, targeted intervention</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AML" target="Care Team">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The care team guides the patient through diagnosis, testing, and therapy selection for acute myeloid leukemia.&lt;SEP&gt;The care team tailors treatment plans and oversees the therapeutic strategy for patients diagnosed with AML.</data>
