    <edge source="Centers for Disease Control and Prevention" target="Smoking and Vaping">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The CDC offers public health resources and cessation guidance to help individuals quit smoking and vaping.</data>
      <data key="d6">health resources, smoking cessation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Smoking and Vaping" target="Head and Neck Cancer Surgery">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Smoking and vaping complicate head and neck cancer surgery by increasing complications, impairing wound healing, and altering anesthesia requirements.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical risk, wound healing</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Smoking and Vaping" target="Lung Function Tests">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Patients with a history of smoking and vaping frequently undergo pulmonary function tests to evaluate respiratory health.</data>
      <data key="d6">pulmonary assessment, respiratory risk</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Smoking and Vaping" target="Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Smoking and vaping increase the risk of serious lung complications during and after chemotherapy treatments.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment risks, pulmonary complications</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mind and Body Therapists" target="Care Team">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
