      <data key="d6">collaborative care, psychological support</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nutritionist or Dietician" target="Care Team">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The care team connects patients with nutritionists or dieticians to ensure proper caloric and fluid intake during therapy.</data>
      <data key="d6">multidisciplinary care, nutritional support</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Anesthesiologist" target="Anesthesia">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The anesthesiologist determines drug dosages and oversees the administration of anesthesia for surgical procedures.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical administration, patient safety</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Anesthesiologist" target="Multidisciplinary Care Team">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">An anesthesiologist supports the team during surgical and invasive procedures by managing patient anesthesia and pain control.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical support, pain management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hepatitis B and Hepatitis C Screening" target="Hepatitis B">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Screening tests identify past or active hepatitis B virus infections to avoid therapy-induced viral reactivation.</data>
      <data key="d6">viral screening, reactivation prevention</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hepatitis B and Hepatitis C Screening" target="Hepatitis C">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Screening blood tests identify hepatitis C virus to protect the liver from treatment-related harm.</data>
      <data key="d6">liver screening, clinical safety</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hepatitis B" target="Hepatocellular Carcinoma">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Hepatitis B virus infection is a major risk factor that directly or through cirrhosis causes liver cancer.")</data>
      <data key="d6">viral etiology, cancer risk</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hepatitis B" target="Cirrhosis">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Hepatitis B infection can cause chronic hepatitis that leads to the scarring of liver tissue known as cirrhosis.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease causation, liver damage</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hepatitis B" target="Liver Cancer Screening">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Patients with chronic hepatitis B are recommended to undergo regular liver cancer screening.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical protocol, disease monitoring</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hepatitis C" target="Hepatocellular Carcinoma">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Hepatitis C virus causes chronic liver damage and cirrhosis, leading to an elevated risk of liver cancer.")</data>
      <data key="d6">viral etiology, disease progression</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hepatitis C" target="Cirrhosis">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Hepatitis C infection can cause chronic liver inflammation, liver failure, and cirrhosis.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease causation, liver scarring</data>
