    </edge>
    <edge source="Human Papillomavirus" target="Anal Cancer">
      <data key="d4">28.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Anal cancer is almost always caused by infection with the human papillomavirus (HPV).&lt;SEP&gt;Infection with high-risk strains of Human Papillomavirus is a major cause of anal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Long-term infection with Human Papillomavirus is the risk factor most strongly linked to the development of anal cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease etiology, viral infection&lt;SEP&gt;oncogenic risk factor, viral etiology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </edge>
