    <edge source="Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia" target="B-ALL">
      <data key="d4">45.0</data>
      <data key="d5">B-ALL is one of the primary immunophenotypic subtypes of acute lymphoblastic leukemia.&lt;SEP&gt;B-ALL is one of the primary subtypes of acute lymphoblastic leukemia, arising from B-cell lymphocytes.&lt;SEP&gt;B-ALL is one of the principal subtypes of acute lymphoblastic leukemia.&lt;SEP&gt;B-ALL is the most prevalent classification of acute lymphoblastic leukemia discussed in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;B-ALL represents one of the two main subtypes of acute lymphoblastic leukemia.</data>
