    <edge source="Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia" target="T-ALL">
      <data key="d4">45.0</data>
      <data key="d5">T-ALL is a recognized subtype of acute lymphoblastic leukemia originating in T-cell lymphocytes.&lt;SEP&gt;T-ALL is a specific subtype of acute lymphoblastic leukemia that originates in T-cell lymphocytes.&lt;SEP&gt;T-ALL represents a specific, less common subtype of acute lymphoblastic leukemia arising from T cells.&lt;SEP&gt;T-ALL represents one of the major forms of acute lymphoblastic leukemia alongside B-ALL.&lt;SEP&gt;T-ALL represents one of the two main subtypes of acute lymphoblastic leukemia.</data>
