    <edge source="Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia" target="Lymphoblasts">
      <data key="d4">38.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Acute lymphoblastic leukemia is characterized by bone marrow producing an excess of immature lymphoblasts.&lt;SEP&gt;An overproduction of abnormal lymphoblasts that crowd bone marrow is the hallmark feature of acute lymphoblastic leukemia.&lt;SEP&gt;In ALL, abnormal lymphoblasts overpopulate and crowd out normal bone marrow cells.&lt;SEP&gt;In acute lymphoblastic leukemia, excessive immature lymphoblasts are produced, crowding out healthy blood cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">pathology, diagnostic hallmark&lt;SEP&gt;pathophysiology, blast cell proliferation&lt;SEP&gt;pathophysiology, leukemic proliferation&lt;SEP&gt;pathophysiology, marrow infiltration</data>
