    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder Cancer" target="Multidisciplinary Care Team">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The multidisciplinary care team collaborates across specialties to treat and manage bladder cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;The multidisciplinary care team collaborates to guide, plan, and administer treatment tailored to the patient's bladder cancer stage.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer treatment, collaborative care&lt;SEP&gt;patient management, clinical coordination</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder Cancer" target="Non-Invasive Bladder Cancer">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Non-invasive bladder cancer is an early, treatable, and often curable stage of bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease classification, early stage</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder Cancer" target="Cystoscopy And Biopsy">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Cystoscopy and biopsy are core diagnostic and evaluation procedures used to inspect and confirm bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic procedures, pathology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder Cancer" target="Imaging">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Imaging tests are used to determine tumor size, invasion depth, and monitor bladder cancer spread.</data>
      <data key="d6">medical imaging, diagnostic staging</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder Cancer" target="Medical And Family Histories">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Medical and family histories help providers identify symptoms, prior treatments, and inherited cancer risks for bladder cancer patients.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical evaluation, risk assessment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder Cancer" target="Urine Cytology">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Urine cytology is used to screen for cancer cells and assist in detecting bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer detection, laboratory test</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder Cancer" target="Biomarker Test">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Biomarker tests analyze urine to identify tumor-shed cells and markers associated with bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">biomarker screening, oncology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder Cancer" target="Doctor">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The doctor evaluates diagnostic findings with the patient to determine ongoing bladder cancer management.</data>
      <data key="d6">patient consultation, care management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder Cancer" target="Diagnostic Imaging">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Diagnostic imaging is utilized to identify the spread, staging, and anatomical location of bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer staging, diagnostic assessment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder Cancer" target="Urogram">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A urogram evaluates the urinary tract lining and helps determine the extent of bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer staging, diagnostic imaging</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder Cancer" target="Germline Testing">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Germline testing is recommended for certain bladder cancer patients to identify inherited mutations like CDKN2A, FGFR3, and PIK3CA.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetic risk, hereditary mutations</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder Cancer" target="Chest Imaging">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Chest imaging with CT or x-ray is performed to determine if bladder cancer has spread to the lungs.</data>
      <data key="d6">metastasis assessment, cancer staging</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder Cancer" target="Urine Test">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Urine tests can reveal blood or abnormal indicators that suggest the presence of bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">symptom detection, disease screening</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder Cancer" target="Vaping">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Vaping can limit the effectiveness of cancer treatments and raise complication risks for bladder cancer patients.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment interference, adverse health outcome</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder Cancer" target="Cancer Staging">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Staging evaluates the physical depth of bladder cancer penetration and its spread to determine the appropriate therapy plan.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease evaluation, clinical classification</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder Cancer" target="Cancer Grading">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Grading determines how aggressive bladder cancer cells are to assist care teams in predicting disease course and treatment response.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease evaluation, cellular pathology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder Cancer" target="Urothelial Layer">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Most bladder cancers originate within the urothelial cells that make up the inner lining of the bladder.</data>
      <data key="d6">cell origin, oncogenesis</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder Cancer" target="TURBT">
      <data key="d4">27.0</data>
      <data key="d5">TURBT is a primary surgical procedure used to diagnose, stage, and remove bladder cancer tumors.&lt;SEP&gt;TURBT is a surgical procedure performed to excise visible tumors in patients with bladder cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;TURBT is performed to diagnose, stage, and remove tumors on the bladder wall in patients with bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnosis and treatment, surgical oncology&lt;SEP&gt;surgical intervention, cancer diagnosis&lt;SEP&gt;surgical treatment, diagnosis</data>
