    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder Cancer" target="Intravesical Therapy">
      <data key="d4">34.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Intravesical therapy delivers cancer medications directly to the bladder wall to treat bladder cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Intravesical therapy is a local bladder cancer treatment option that delivers liquid medication directly into the bladder.&lt;SEP&gt;Intravesical therapy is applied directly to the bladder as a targeted treatment for bladder cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Intravesical therapy is directly administered into the bladder to manage and treat bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">localized therapy, oncological treatment&lt;SEP&gt;medical treatment, oncology protocol&lt;SEP&gt;oncological treatment, localized therapy&lt;SEP&gt;targeted treatment, oncology therapy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder Cancer" target="Systemic Therapy">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
