    </edge>
    <edge source="Early-Stage Prostate Cancer" target="Advanced-Stage Prostate Cancer">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Early-stage and advanced-stage represent distinct stages of prostate cancer progression based on whether the cancer has spread beyond the prostate gland.&lt;SEP&gt;Early-stage and advanced-stage represent the two primary disease classifications of prostate cancer based on spread beyond the prostate.</data>
      <data key="d6">comparative staging, progression&lt;SEP&gt;disease staging, progression</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Early-Stage Prostate Cancer" target="Active Surveillance">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Active surveillance is an initial management option for patients with early-stage prostate cancer to monitor the disease without immediate aggressive treatment.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease management, monitoring</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Early-Stage Prostate Cancer" target="Surgery">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Surgery is one of the primary treatment options available for patients diagnosed with early-stage prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment option, curative care</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Early-Stage Prostate Cancer" target="Radiation Therapy">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Radiation therapy is a common treatment choice utilized to treat early-stage prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment option, therapeutic intervention</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Early-Stage Prostate Cancer" target="Hormone Therapy">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
