    </edge>
    <edge source="Prostate" target="Prostate-Specific Antigen">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The prostate gland produces prostate-specific antigen (PSA) to nourish and help transmit semen.</data>
      <data key="d6">protein production, secretion</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Prostate" target="Semen">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The prostate produces fluid that makes up a significant part of semen.</data>
      <data key="d6">fluid secretion, reproduction</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Prostate" target="Urethra">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The prostate wraps around the urethra just beneath the bladder.</data>
      <data key="d6">anatomical structure, proximity</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Prostate" target="Bladder">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The prostate is positioned just beneath the bladder.</data>
      <data key="d6">anatomical proximity</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Prostate-Specific Antigen" target="Prostate Gland">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The prostate gland produces prostate-specific antigen (PSA), which can increase if the prostate has abnormalities.</data>
      <data key="d6">biological production, organ function</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Semen" target="Seminal Vesicles">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The seminal vesicles produce fluid that combines with secretions from the prostate and sperm to form semen.</data>
      <data key="d6">fluid secretion, reproduction</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Urethra" target="Bladder">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The urethra carries urine from the bladder out of the body.</data>
      <data key="d6">anatomical connection, urinary function</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Urethra" target="Prostate Gland">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The prostate surrounds the urethra, meaning prostate enlargement or tumors can compress the urethra and restrict urine flow.</data>
      <data key="d6">anatomical structure, urinary function</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder" target="Prostate Gland">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The prostate gland is located immediately below the bladder in the pelvic cavity.</data>
      <data key="d6">anatomical proximity, urinary system</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Seminal Vesicles" target="Prostate Gland">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The prostate and seminal vesicles both produce fluids that combine with sperm to form semen.</data>
      <data key="d6">reproductive anatomy, fluid production</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Metastatic Prostate Cancer" target="Targeted Therapy">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Targeted therapy is applied as a specialized treatment option for qualifying cases of metastatic prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Targeted therapy is evaluated as a treatment option for patients diagnosed with metastatic prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer therapy, advanced disease&lt;SEP&gt;oncological treatment, precision oncology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Metastatic Prostate Cancer" target="Biopsy of the Metastasis">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A biopsy of metastatic sites confirms whether cancer has spread beyond the prostate to lymph nodes, bones, or organs.</data>
      <data key="d6">metastasis diagnosis, disease staging</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Early Detection Screening" target="Black Males">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Because of higher disease severity and earlier onset, Black males are advised to consult providers about earlier screening tests.&lt;SEP&gt;Early detection screening is particularly emphasized for Black males due to higher risks of aggressive prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">preventive healthcare, early diagnosis&lt;SEP&gt;targeted screening, disparity mitigation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Early Detection Screening" target="Health Care Providers">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Health care providers administer and consult with patients regarding early detection screening tests for prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Health care providers administer and recommend screening tests to catch prostate cancer early.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical care, patient consultation&lt;SEP&gt;preventive medicine, clinical screening</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Black Males" target="White Males">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Black males are twice as likely to die from prostate cancer and more likely to develop it at an earlier and more aggressive stage compared to white males.</data>
      <data key="d6">comparative health risk, racial disparity</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Black Males" target="Hispanic Males">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Hispanic males have lower prostate cancer incidence rates compared to Black males.</data>
      <data key="d6">demographic disparity, incidence rates</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Black Males" target="Asian Males">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Asian males are diagnosed with prostate cancer less frequently than Black males.</data>
      <data key="d6">demographic disparity, incidence comparison</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Black Males" target="Health Care Providers">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Black males are advised to consult health care providers about earlier and more frequent screening tests.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical consultation, preventive care</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Black Males" target="Researchers">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Researchers are actively studying the causes of health disparities and differing disease outcomes observed in Black males.</data>
      <data key="d6">medical research, health disparity investigation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="White Males" target="Hispanic Males">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Hispanic males are diagnosed with prostate cancer less frequently than white males.</data>
      <data key="d6">demographic comparison, cancer incidence</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="White Males" target="Asian Males">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Asian males show lower rates of prostate cancer diagnosis in comparison to white males.</data>
      <data key="d6">incidence comparison, demographics</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Health Care Providers" target="Prostate Cancer Screening Tests">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
