    <edge source="Screening Mammogram" target="Diagnostic Mammogram">
      <data key="d4">23.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A diagnostic mammogram provides more detailed imaging than a standard screening mammogram.&lt;SEP&gt;Diagnostic mammograms are used to follow up on abnormal findings identified during routine screening mammograms.&lt;SEP&gt;Diagnostic mammograms are utilized to provide a closer examination of abnormal areas identified during screening mammograms.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic differentiation, breast imaging&lt;SEP&gt;follow-up testing, diagnostic escalation&lt;SEP&gt;follow-up, diagnostic comparison</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Screening Mammogram" target="Imaging Tests">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Screening mammograms are an imaging test conducted routinely to screen for breast abnormalities.</data>
      <data key="d6">medical imaging, diagnostic categorization</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Diagnostic Mammogram" target="Biopsy">
      <data key="d4">15.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Biopsies and diagnostic mammograms are complementary diagnostic procedures used to detect and confirm breast cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Diagnostic mammography is a key imaging step that helps determine the necessity of a biopsy for breast cancer evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic pathway, clinical investigation&lt;SEP&gt;diagnostic workup, cancer detection</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Diagnostic Mammogram" target="Imaging Tests">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Diagnostic mammograms represent an imaging test used to closely inspect breast symptoms or abnormalities.&lt;SEP&gt;Diagnostic mammography is a standard imaging tool, though its findings may be subtle or absent in inflammatory breast cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">medical imaging, diagnostic categorization&lt;SEP&gt;radiology, diagnostic screening</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Diagnostic Mammogram" target="Tomosynthesis">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Diagnostic mammograms may utilize 3D tomosynthesis imaging technology to generate detailed pictures of breast tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;Tomosynthesis, or 3D mammogram technology, is utilized in performing detailed diagnostic breast evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d6">imaging technology, diagnostic procedure&lt;SEP&gt;technological application, breast imaging</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Diagnostic Mammogram" target="Breast MRI">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A breast MRI may be used alongside or in addition to a mammogram for comprehensive evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d6">complementary imaging, diagnostic support</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Diagnostic Mammogram" target="Bilateral Mammogram">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A bilateral mammogram is a mammographic examination evaluating both breasts to assist in planning medical treatment.</data>
      <data key="d6">mammography subtype, treatment planning</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
    </edge>
