    <edge source="Primary CNS Lymphoma" target="Imaging Tests">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Imaging tests such as MRI and CT scans are key diagnostic tools used to evaluate and detect primary CNS lymphoma.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic imaging, medical evaluation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Primary CNS Lymphoma" target="Neurological Exam">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A neurological exam is an essential diagnostic evaluation conducted to identify focal neurological deficits caused by primary CNS lymphoma.&lt;SEP&gt;A neurological exam is an initial assessment conducted to identify neurological deficits caused by primary CNS lymphoma.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnosis, clinical examination&lt;SEP&gt;preliminary assessment, clinical examination</data>
