    </edge>
    <edge source="Papillary Thyroid Carcinoma" target="Classic Type Papillary Thyroid Cancer">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Classic type is the most common histological variant of papillary thyroid carcinoma.</data>
      <data key="d6">subtype classification, histology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Papillary Thyroid Carcinoma" target="Tall-Cell/Columnar Cell Carcinoma">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Tall-cell/columnar cell carcinoma is a higher-risk subtype of papillary thyroid cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">subtype classification, clinical aggression</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Papillary Thyroid Carcinoma" target="Hobnail Variant">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Hobnail variant is an aggressive histological subtype of papillary thyroid cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">subtype classification, clinical aggression</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Papillary Thyroid Carcinoma" target="Diffuse Sclerosing Variant">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Diffuse sclerosing variant is a subtype of papillary thyroid cancer capable of rapid spread.</data>
      <data key="d6">subtype classification, clinical aggression</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Papillary Thyroid Carcinoma" target="Follicular Variant of Papillary Thyroid Cancer">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Follicular variant is a specific morphological subtype of papillary thyroid carcinoma.</data>
      <data key="d6">subtype classification, histology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Completion Thyroidectomy" target="Pathologist">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Pathologic evaluation identifying high-risk or invasive tumor features prompts the recommendation for completion thyroidectomy.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic evaluation, surgical indication</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NIFTP" target="Papillary Thyroid Cancer">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">NIFTP was previously classified as the encapsulated follicular variant of papillary thyroid cancer before being reclassified as a low-risk neoplasm.</data>
      <data key="d6">reclassification, tumor taxonomy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Neck Ultrasound" target="No Evidence Of Disease">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Patients with no evidence of disease undergo long-term periodic surveillance that includes neck ultrasound imaging.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer surveillance, clinical status</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Recurrence" target="Biomarker Testing">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Biomarker testing is recommended for recurrent thyroid cancer that cannot be treated with RAI therapy.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic protocol, treatment selection</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Recurrence" target="Targeted Therapy">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Targeted therapy is recommended for recurrent thyroid cancer that is unresectable, non-responsive to RAI, and progressing.</data>
      <data key="d6">pharmacotherapy, cancer treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Recurrence" target="Radiation Therapy">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Radiation therapy is an option for treating neck recurrences that are unresectable and do not respond to RAI therapy.</data>
      <data key="d6">locoregional therapy, recurrence management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Recurrence" target="Lenvatinib">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Lenvatinib is the preferred targeted drug for progressive recurrence that cannot be surgically resected and does not absorb iodine.</data>
      <data key="d6">targeted therapy, systemic treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Recurrence" target="Clinical Trial">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Participation in a clinical trial is strongly advised when established therapies for recurrent thyroid cancer fail or are unavailable.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical research, treatment alternative</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Recurrence" target="Abdominoperineal Resection (APR)">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Abdominoperineal resection is recommended when anal cancer recurs locally in the anal area.</data>
      <data key="d6">salvage surgery, recurrence management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Recurrence" target="Metastatic Anal Cancer">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Cancer recurrence can manifest as metastatic anal cancer when it returns in distant organs such as the liver or lungs.</data>
      <data key="d6">distant relapse, disease spread</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid-Stimulating Hormone" target="No Evidence Of Disease">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">TSH blood testing is a standard component of long-term surveillance for patients with no evidence of disease.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer surveillance, laboratory monitoring</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroglobulin" target="Anti-Thyroglobulin Antibodies">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Anti-thyroglobulin antibodies interfere with thyroglobulin blood test accuracy, requiring simultaneous measurement.</data>
      <data key="d6">laboratory assessment, interference</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lenvatinib" target="Cabozantinib">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Cabozantinib is recommended as next-line treatment if thyroid cancer progresses following therapy with lenvatinib.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment sequence, targeted therapy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Cancer" target="Chordoma">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Chordoma is categorized and addressed as a distinct type of bone cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Chordoma is covered as a distinct primary bone tumor affecting spinal and skull regions.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease taxonomy, oncology classification&lt;SEP&gt;tumor type, clinical classification</data>
