      <data key="d7">chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Cancer" target="Care Team">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The care team collaborates with patients to diagnose, stage, and deliver personalized treatment plans for rare bone cancers.</data>
      <data key="d6">medical treatment, patient care, multidisciplinary team</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Cancer" target="Biomarker Testing">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Biomarker testing is utilized in testing for bone cancer to characterize the biological behavior of the tumor.</data>
      <data key="d6">oncologic diagnosis, biomarker analysis</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Cancer" target="Bone Cancer Staging">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Staging evaluates the anatomical location and spread of tumors to guide bone cancer management.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease staging, clinical evaluation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Cancer" target="Imaging Tests">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Imaging tests are essential tools used in diagnosing, localizing, and evaluating bone cancer lesions.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic imaging, tumor detection</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Cancer" target="Biopsy">
      <data key="d4">27.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A biopsy procedure is required to confirm the diagnosis of bone cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A biopsy, such as a core needle or surgical biopsy, is required to confirm a diagnosis of bone cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Biopsies provide tissue samples necessary for accurate diagnosis and staging of primary bone cancers.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic procedure, cancer diagnosis&lt;SEP&gt;medical diagnosis, clinical testing&lt;SEP&gt;tissue biopsy, histopathology, diagnosis</data>
