      <data key="d6">genetic disorder, liver pathology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Cirrhosis" target="Liver Cancer Screening">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Individuals diagnosed with cirrhosis are recommended to be routinely enrolled in liver cancer screening programs.&lt;SEP&gt;Patients diagnosed with cirrhosis are advised to enroll in regular liver cancer screening to detect malignancy early.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical protocol, high-risk screening&lt;SEP&gt;risk indication, clinical screening</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Cirrhosis" target="Primary Biliary Cholangitis">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Stage 4 primary biliary cholangitis is identified as a direct cause and precursor of cirrhosis.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease progression, liver pathology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Cirrhosis" target="Alpha-1-Antitrypsin Deficiency">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Alpha-1-antitrypsin deficiency is a recognized underlying cause contributing to liver cirrhosis.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetic disorder, liver pathology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Liver Cancer Screening" target="Alpha-Fetoprotein Test">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The alpha-fetoprotein (AFP) blood test is a standard routine examination used alongside ultrasound in liver cancer screening.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic marker, clinical screening</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Liver Cancer Screening" target="Chronic Hepatitis B">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Chronic hepatitis B status prompts enrollment into regular liver cancer screening programs.</data>
      <data key="d6">risk indication, clinical screening</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Liver Cancer" target="Imaging Tests">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Imaging tests serve as the primary diagnostic tool used to confirm liver cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease confirmation, clinical diagnosis</data>
