    </edge>
    <edge source="Glioma" target="Radiation Therapy">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Radiation therapy is a core treatment utilized to slow down glioma progression and manage symptoms.&lt;SEP&gt;Radiation therapy is a primary treatment modality utilized to stabilize and control glioma tumors.</data>
      <data key="d6">medical treatment, therapy&lt;SEP&gt;oncological treatment, disease management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Glioma" target="Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Chemotherapy is a standard treatment modality often combined with surgery and radiation to suppress glioma growth.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy is an established treatment used to stop or stabilize glioma growth.</data>
      <data key="d6">medical treatment, oncology&lt;SEP&gt;pharmacological therapy, disease control</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
