    <edge source="Biopsy" target="Imaging Tests">
      <data key="d4">32.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Imaging tests can be performed prior to, during, or after a biopsy to guide sampling and verify findings.&lt;SEP&gt;Imaging tests can precede a biopsy, guide needle placement during the biopsy, or follow it to determine tumor extent and staging.&lt;SEP&gt;Results from both imaging tests and biopsy work together to establish clinical cancer stage and treatment plans.&lt;SEP&gt;Ultrasound or CT scans are imaging tools utilized to guide lymph node biopsies.</data>
