      <data key="d5">Doctors are key members of the multidisciplinary care team overseeing patient evaluations and treatment plans.&lt;SEP&gt;Doctors serve as primary medical practitioners and communicators within the patient's multidisciplinary care team.&lt;SEP&gt;Doctors serve as the primary clinical communicators and decision-makers within the patient's multidisciplinary care team.&lt;SEP&gt;The doctor collaborates within the care team to discuss diagnostic findings with the patient.&lt;SEP&gt;The doctor is a core clinical professional within the patient's cancer care team.&lt;SEP&gt;The doctor is a core member of the broader clinical care team responsible for treating the patient.&lt;SEP&gt;The doctor operates as a central member of the care team providing clinical evaluations and management.&lt;SEP&gt;The patient's doctor collaborates within the medical team to formulate diagnostic and treatment pathways.</data>
